{"name":"Blobfish","hex":"#d0b8bf","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blobfish","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Psychrolutes marcidus, a fish that inhabits the deep waters off the coasts of the Australian mainland and Tasmania."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blobfish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Psychrolutidae","blocks":[{"text":"Psychrolutidae is a family of sculpins found in cool temperate waters throughout the Northern Hemisphere, with a few species ranging into cold and deep waters of the Southern Hemisphere. The vast majority are found in marine habitats, but a few range into freshwater habitats. The family reaches its greatest diversity in the North Pacific Ocean, but a few species are found as far south as Antarctica. The family contains over 216 recognized species in 63 genera. Their name is derived from the Greek psychrolouteo, meaning \"to have a cold bath\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Oligocottus_maculosus_317361085.jpg/330px-Oligocottus_maculosus_317361085.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychrolutidae","wikidata":"Q1210085"},{"title":"Psychrolutes microporos","blocks":[{"text":"Psychrolutes microporos is a species of deepwater marine fish in the family Psychrolutidae, commonly known as a blobfish or fathead. It is found in the abyssal zone in waters around Australia and New Zealand. A photograph of an individual taken in 2003 has become famous on the internet for its appearance, widely viewed as unsightly."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychrolutes_microporos","wikidata":"Q2912702"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Psychrolutes_phrictus_1.jpg/500px-Psychrolutes_phrictus_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Psychrolutes_phrictus_1.jpg/500px-Psychrolutes_phrictus_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APsychrolutes_phrictus_1.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Myoxocephalinae - Andøy, Norway 2023-07-12 (02)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Myoxocephalinae_-_And%C3%B8y%2C_Norway_2023-07-12_%2802%29.jpg/500px-Myoxocephalinae_-_And%C3%B8y%2C_Norway_2023-07-12_%2802%29.jpg","ratio":1.778712390812035,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myoxocephalinae_-_And%C3%B8y,_Norway_2023-07-12_(02).jpg","share":0.32},{"title":"Myoxocephalinae - Andøy, Norway 2023-07-12 (01)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Myoxocephalinae_-_And%C3%B8y%2C_Norway_2023-07-12_%2801%29.jpg/500px-Myoxocephalinae_-_And%C3%B8y%2C_Norway_2023-07-12_%2801%29.jpg","ratio":1.7795648060548723,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myoxocephalinae_-_And%C3%B8y,_Norway_2023-07-12_(01).jpg","share":0.249375},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.24625},{"title":"FMIB 52141 Gilbertidia sigolutes (Jordan) Puget Sound","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/FMIB_52141_Gilbertidia_sigolutes_%28Jordan%29_Puget_Sound.jpeg/500px-FMIB_52141_Gilbertidia_sigolutes_%28Jordan%29_Puget_Sound.jpeg","ratio":3.2135593220338983,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FMIB_52141_Gilbertidia_sigolutes_(Jordan)_Puget_Sound.jpeg","share":0.195},{"title":"FMIB 39347 Dasycottus setiger bean","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/FMIB_39347_Dasycottus_setiger_bean.jpeg/500px-FMIB_39347_Dasycottus_setiger_bean.jpeg","ratio":3.079510703363914,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File: